                         difficulty, answer_status, content_key, origin)
    VALUES (subj, tid, 'A soft-iron toroid is concentric with a long straight conductor carrying a direct current $I$. If the relative permeability $\mur$ of soft-iron is 100, the...', 'A soft-iron toroid is concentric with a long straight conductor carrying a direct current $I$. If the relative permeability
$\mu_r$ of soft-iron is 100, the ratio of the magnetic flux densities at two adjacent points located just inside and just outside
the toroid, is _______.
', '**Idea used:** around a long straight wire, $H$ goes round in circles with $H = \dfrac{I}{2\pi r}$ (Ampère''s law), whatever the
material. Then $B = \mu H = \mu_0\mu_r H$.

1. The toroid is concentric with the wire, so $H$ is along the iron''s surface (tangential). The tangential $H$ is the same just
   inside and just outside (boundary condition, no surface current).
2. Inside the iron: $B_{in} = \mu_0 \times 100 \times H$. Just outside (air): $B_{out} = \mu_0 \times 1 \times H$.
3. Ratio $B_{in} / B_{out} = 100$.

**Without a calculator:** same $H$ on both sides of the boundary, so the flux densities differ only by $\mu_r$. Answer 100.
(Option B is the ratio upside down.)

**Answer: 100.**
', 'READY', 'NAT', 99, 101, 2, 'OFFICIAL_KEY', 'gate2016-s1-q14', 'PYQ') RETURNING id INTO qid;
